<br/>
<br/>These are all fairly standard choices so you shouldn't see too many surprises. We've grabbed our two-piece bonus here but that isn't too strong either - it's just a very minor stat difference to wearing no pieces at all. We've reforged spirit to crit on our Haste pieces here but they are similar in value and you can skip that step if you'd like.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="what-were-looking-for">What we're looking for</h5>
<i>
<span class="q7">Intellect &gt; Haste &gt; Crit = Spirit &gt; Mastery </span></i>
<br/>Your primary goal when gearing is to get as much Intellect as possible. Fortunately, we can do that by picking our highest item level gear in most cases. We'll also want to equip at least two pieces of our new tier set though neither of our bonuses are very exciting.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="where-to-get-gear">Where to get gear</h5>Given this is a Best in Slot list, you'll find a lot of the items on it drop from raid. If you're not intending on raiding then the pre-raid Best in slot page might be a better fit for you. In either case you're going to farm a lot of Elemental Twilight Dungeons since a lot of the drops and items you can buy with the resulting currency are very powerful. Use this gear to start yourself off and to fill slots later in the tier.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="priority-pieces">Priority Pieces</h5>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78476/maw-of-the-dragonlord">
<img alt="Maw of the Dragonlord" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_1h_deathwingraiddw_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Maw of the Dragonlord</span></a> is a godly weapon for all scenarios where healing is relevant. You are also able to weapon swap it mid-fight if you have <a class="q5 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71086/dragonwrath-tarecgosas-rest">
<img alt="Dragonwrath, Tarecgosa's Rest" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/stave_2h_tarecgosa_e_01stagefinal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dragonwrath, Tarecgosa's Rest</span></a> and want to swap between adding damage and healing which is particularly interesting on a fight like Ultraxion. Grab it early. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77975/will-of-unbinding">
<img alt="Will of Unbinding" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_stonetablet_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Will of Unbinding</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77996/heart-of-unliving">
<img alt="Heart of Unliving" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_qirajicrystal_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Unliving</span></a> are also tremendous and priority picks for your fragments.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="spending-valor">Spending Valor</h5>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> is a type of Raid currency that you get from killing bosses in Raids and completing Heroic Dungeons through the Random Dungeon Finder tool. The vendors you can exchange these at are <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=46556/jamusvaz">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Jamus'Vaz</span></a> for the Horde and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=44245/faldren-tillsdale">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Faldren Tillsdale</span></a> for the Alliance. You can use <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> to obtain relevant catch-up gear to get you ready for Dragon Soul as soon as possible. <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> gear is quite well itemized this tier and you have several good choices. The order in which you pick pieces is a bit dependent on what gear you already have but I'll make recommendations for a few different scenarios.<br/>
<br/>You will use <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77096/woundlicker-cover">
<img alt="Woundlicker Cover" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_deathwingraid_d_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Woundlicker Cover</span></a> all tier since Dragon Soul doesn't actually drop any capes. If you want a slot you can buy and then lock in until next expansion then it's not a bad start. <br/>
<br/>If Heroic isn't on the cards early then <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77089/threadlinked-chain">
<img alt="Threadlinked Chain" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_necklace_35.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Threadlinked Chain</span></a> beats all non-heroic alternatives with its perfect itemization. For your other <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> choices, aim to maximize how much item level you are gaining. Avoid low-value pieces like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77114/bottled-wishes">
<img alt="Bottled Wishes" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_potion_109.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bottled Wishes</span></a> and be cautious buying items in tier slots since you might not use them long. Outside of <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77096/woundlicker-cover">
<img alt="Woundlicker Cover" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_deathwingraid_d_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Woundlicker Cover</span></a>, think of <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> as catch up gear to help you patch up rough slots.<br/>
<br/>
