<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="trinkets-for-discipline-priest-healer">Trinkets for Discipline Priest Healer</h4>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77995/will-of-unbinding">
<img alt="Will of Unbinding" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_stonetablet_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Will of Unbinding</span></a> is bolted into trinket slot one. As a healer that casts a lot of DPS spells we're able to keep it stacked to 10 very easily and at max stacks it is by far the best trinket in the game. Even during periods of very high damage where you might be casting a lot of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=596/prayer-of-healing">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_prayerofhealing02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Prayer of Healing</span></a>, the trinket is strong enough to justify including one DPS spell every 10 seconds. Your second slot has somewhat more choice. If a fight encourages you to spend all of your mana then <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77996/heart-of-unliving">
<img alt="Heart of Unliving" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_qirajicrystal_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Unliving</span></a> is extremely overbudget and a clear choice for your second slot. On fights that are <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=81749/atonement">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_priest_atonement.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Atonement</span></a> heavy (or lacking in damage entirely) you could run <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77989/seal-of-the-seven-signs">
<img alt="Seal of the Seven Signs" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_relics_runestone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Seal of the Seven Signs</span></a>, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=77991/insignia-of-the-corrupted-mind">
<img alt="Insignia of the Corrupted Mind" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bijou_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Insignia of the Corrupted Mind</span></a> or even a full DPS trinket instead.<div class="pad"></div>
