<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="weapons">Weapons for Discipline Priest Healer</h3>
<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="main-hand-weapons-for-discipline-priest-healer">Main Hand Weapons for Discipline Priest Healer</h4>There is only a single one-handed weapon you will ever equip: <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78485/maw-of-the-dragonlord">
<img alt="Maw of the Dragonlord" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_1h_deathwingraiddw_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Maw of the Dragonlord</span></a> and lower item level versions of it. Buy the LFR version as soon as you can and then upgrade it when able. Maw is an absurd HPS increase but for fights or even phases where there's nothing to heal, you can wear a DPS weapon like <a class="q5 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71086/dragonwrath-tarecgosas-rest">
<img alt="Dragonwrath, Tarecgosa's Rest" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/stave_2h_tarecgosa_e_01stagefinal.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dragonwrath, Tarecgosa's Rest</span></a> or eventually a Heroic <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=78477/titahk-the-steps-of-time">
<img alt="Ti'tahk, the Steps of Time" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stave_2h_deathwingraiddw_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ti'tahk, the Steps of Time</span></a> (though neither are 1 handers). As general advice though I'd lean on the healing weapon more frequently than the DPS weapon but higher end players might benefit a lot from weapon swapping during a fight.<br/>
